  "query_preview": "..\nKEY MESSAGE 1...The threat for flooding has diminished tonight,\nalthough scattered showers will linger along and north of the \nI-78 corridor into the overnight hours.\n\nThe warm front is now northwest of the I-95 corridor, and will \ncontinue to lift north tonight through Thursday morning. Most of\nthe heavy rain has tapered off, but there are still some\nscattered showers, perhaps a rumble of thunder, that will \nimpact areas along and north of the I-78 corridor into the\novernight hours. Brief, locally heavy rain will continue to be \npossible, though the threat for flooding has diminished.\n\nOtherwise, quite warm and humid tonight with patchy fog \ndeveloping across the region. Lows tonight will be in the low to\nmid 70s, and dewpoints will be right around that as well.\n\n\nKEY MESSAGE 2...Hot and humid conditions into early next week. \nHeat Advisory issued for portions of the area for Thursday and \nFriday.\n\nOnce the warm front lifts north of the area, our area will be \nunder the influence of high pressure located offshore of the \nAtlantic seaboard, which will lead to well established return \nflow. This will keep hot and humid conditions in place for the \nnext several days. A Heat Advisory has been issued for all areas\nwho's criteria is heat index values of 100-104 degrees. This \nincludes portions of eastern Pennsylvania, much of New Jersey \nexcept the far southern counties, as well as New Castle Delware.\nThe Heat Advisory will run from 10 am Thursday and continue \nthrough 8 pm Friday.",
